From ed5d85de4d8124ea1f60b9c07c9abb2c5d8f5633 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:15:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(geometry): import DXF splines and ellipses as
 tangent arcs

The DXF reader reads SPLINE (degree, knots, control points, weights,
fit-point count) and ELLIPSE (centre, major axis, ratio, parameters)
and lays each as tangent-continuous biarcs and lines within a checked
two-sided bound of 1 um (CURVE_TOLERANCE_MM). Arcs above 1000 mm
radius become lines. An ellipse with ratio 1 stays an exact circle or
arc. Malformed data (knots, weights, counts, degree, ratio, sweep,
planes) is refused by name; the work per drawing is budgeted.

INSERT and POINT are skipped and counted, so the rest of the drawing
reads. A selected-chain wire cut still refuses them by name, as HATCH.

SketchData refuses a drawing whose curves were read for a smaller
unit than the applied one (CurveTolerance).

Provenance lines of the native Agie post no longer name the tool they
came from; they say "our own implementation".

The wire_dxf_selection arcs suite carries the start-pick fix of #3953
so that it builds on main.

Refs #3937
Refs #1865

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
