@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 
 **Decided: refuse bad data by name, never clamp.** Refused: degree outside 1 to 11; a knot count that is not points + degree + 1; knots that are not finite or decrease; an empty domain; a knot multiplicity that breaks the curve; a weight count that differs from the point count; a weight that is zero, negative or not finite; weights that differ by more than 1e6; control points in more than one Z plane; counts over the vertex limit (checked before the values are read); fit points without control points (interpolation is not implemented); an ellipse ratio outside (0, 1]; a zero major axis; a zero sweep; a parameter over 1e6; a tilted axis or extrusion. A curve that needs more evaluations than the drawing budget (50 million) is refused before the work starts. A cusp that 40 halvings cannot fit is refused by name.
 
-**Decided: an ellipse with ratio 1 stays exact.** It becomes a `Circle` or an `Arc`, with no fit. A degree-1 spline becomes its control polygon (it is split at each corner knot).
+**Decided: an ellipse with ratio 1 stays exact; a near-round one is a circle only within the bound.** Ratio 1 becomes a `Circle` or an `Arc`, with no fit and no recorded tolerance. Below 1, the circle of radius a is at most a (1 - ratio) from the ellipse. The reader uses the circle only when that distance is within the tolerance in drawing units, and then records the tolerance on the document. Otherwise it fits arcs. Dropped: a fixed ratio threshold (1e-12). At a radius of 1e10 mm it let a 0.005 mm error through (review of PR #3958). A degree-1 spline becomes its control polygon (it is split at each corner knot).
 
 **Decided: INSERT and POINT no longer stop the import.** An INSERT is skipped and counted (its ATTRIB records up to SEQEND are read with it). A POINT is skipped and counted. The rest of the drawing is read. Block expansion stays open on #1865. Why: one block reference or one point should not stop a drawing whose profile is plain geometry. A selected-chain wire cut still refuses a drawing with a skipped INSERT or POINT by name ("skipped 1 INSERT entity whose clearance from the wire cannot be checked"), as for HATCH. The geometry of a block is not read, so no chain can use it, and the clearance of the wire from it cannot be checked. Dropped: treating POINT as annotation for the wire cut. That changes the path note text of #3937 and its goldens.
 

From 1359ef98efa6a74c6e01b27054194f02750bae78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Quintin Smits <qd.smits@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:41:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(geometry): validate each DXF spline fit point
 elevation

The fit points (group codes 11/21/31) now follow the control point
rule of 62b3fdf17: one Z for each point, an omitted Z is 0, an orphan
or duplicate Z is refused, and all fit and control points are in one
Z plane, else the SPLINE is refused by name.

Refs #1865

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
